    {
      "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bf6424c41beb0065a6cc6618ae3c054fe71fcc1b.001.1",
      "event": "Flood Watch",
      "severity": "Severe",
      "urgency": "Future",
      "certainty": "Possible",
      "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 27 at 2:54AM HST until October 29 at 5:00AM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "A trough moving over the state will bring abundant tropical moisture\ntoday through at least Wednesday night. Heavy rain and isolated\nthunderstorms are expected to produce flash flooding, and while the\ngreatest flood threat will be focused over Oahu and Maui County, all\nislands are at risk.\n\n* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...All main Hawaiian Islands.\n\n* WHEN...From 6 AM HST this morning through late Wednesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Significant flooding may occur due to the overflow of\nstreams and drainages. Roads in several areas may be closed, along\nwith property damage in urban or low lying spots due to runoff.\nLandslides may also occur in areas with steep terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Heavy showers and isolated thunderstorms with intense rain rates\nare expected to develop today and continue through Wednesday\nnight as a trough moves over the state. While the greatest flood\nthreat will be focused over Oahu and Maui County, all islands are\nat risk.",
      "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
